2026-10-09T19:43:03.6214854Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6224730Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6225683Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6226154Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6226347Z 
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6226541Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6226767Z 
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6227031Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6227454Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6227661Z 
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6227777Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6228076Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6228252Z 
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6228445Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T19:43:03.6228804Z   $ sh ./install-nix
